                <pb facs="0169" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4626: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Personal Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-17T14:00:00-05:00">January 17, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Batista has just sent me word that in view of the very precarious strike
                    situation (seriously endangering enormous American properties) provoked by
                    Guiteras and also in view of Hevia’s inability to secure the full support of
                    Mendieta group he has decided to declare Mendieta President this afternoon. He
                    may meet with armed resistance from the Cuban Navy.</p>
                <p>I do not know that this decision is final but he says now that he has
                    decided.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
